Pako Engineers - Thread Profile and Tolerance Guide

Precision lock nuts and threaded components are machined with controlled thread form, pitch, and face alignment.

Typical capability:
- Outside diameter: 30 mm to 750 mm
- Thread forms: metric, Whitworth, Acme, trapezoidal, left-hand, right-hand, and custom
- Pitch range: 1 mm to 120 mm
- Face runout: within 0.02 mm
- Locking features: spanner slots, grub screw holes, castle slots, and custom retention features

Threads are checked using calibrated gauges, pitch measurement, and drawing-based inspection.
